# sepolicy.rule
#
# Custom SELinux policy rules for microG Minimal.
#
# Android 9+ executes priv-app system applications under standard SELinux
# domains (system_file / privapp_data_file). Because microG APKs are mounted
# directly into system/priv-app (Go layout) and system/product/priv-app
# (standard layout) with standard 0644 permissions and inherit standard
# priv-app SELinux contexts, no custom type transitions, capability grants,
# or permissive rules are required.
#
# This file is intentionally left without active rules to avoid broadening
# SELinux permissions unnecessarily.
